---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const habits=[["01","Start with the question","Requirements are clues, not always the whole problem. I try to understand who needs the change and what a useful result would look like."],["02","Choose for the situation","Frameworks, patterns and abstractions are trade-offs. The right choice depends on constraints, team familiarity, future change and the cost of complexity."],["03","Make the work inspectable","Small increments, clear decisions and tests make it easier to see what changed and catch what did not behave as expected."],["04","Be honest about the result","A feature is not finished because its code exists. I check the behaviour that matters, record limitations and distinguish what is working from what is still an assumption."]];
---
<SiteLayout title="Engineering approach — Osama Ibrahim" description="Some working habits behind Osama Ibrahim's engineering decisions.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><small class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING APPROACH / WORKING NOTES</small><h1>There is no single<br/>right way to <em>build.</em></h1><p>These are a few habits I return to. They are not a universal process, and not every project needs the same sequence.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container approach editorial-approach">{habits.map(([n,title,desc])=><article data-reveal><b>{n}</b><div><h2>{title}</h2><p>{desc}</p></div><span>↗</span></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="statement"><div class="container"><small class="eyebrow">A NOTE ON QUALITY</small><h2>Make the result useful. Make the reasoning <em>visible.</em> Be clear about what remains.</h2><a class="button light" href="/projects/">See how that looks in practice ↗</a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
